From e6d1326c2b7a86bcbecd0bac0c677c94a737b545 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini experiment <experiment@invalid>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:49:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: let the scan ignore a BSS absence or presence
 notice

The third lifecycle boot re-armed after its first lifetime and admitted
the second scan, which the firmware answered 28 ms later with a 12-byte
EVENT_ID_BSS_ABSENCE_PRESENCE notice for the BSS it had just torn down.
The scan's event consumer knows the done header, the debug event and the
sleepy notification only, so it refused the notice as a protocol fault,
retired the scan, and the join that followed was refused for lack of a
scan. The first lifetime never sees this notice because its scan runs
before any BSS exists. Admit the notice in the scan consumer as the join
path already does: log its four body bytes once and continue to the
scan's own completion. Every other event the scan does not know stays a
fault.

Internal experiment archive; synthetic non-certifying author,
not submission-ready.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c
index b4ad67553..87d3d155b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c
@@ -1291,6 +1291,20 @@ static int mt6797_mac_scan_packet(struct mt6797_mac *mac, size_t bytes,
 			if (ret)
 				return ret;
 			return own & BIT(8) ? 0 : -EACCES;
+		case 0x11:
+			/* EVENT_ID_BSS_ABSENCE_PRESENCE: an unsolicited notice the
+			 * firmware emits for a BSS it still tracks. The second
+			 * lifetime's scan receives the previous BSS's notice here;
+			 * it is a state change the scan does not depend on, so it
+			 * is logged (four body bytes, no address fits) and ignored,
+			 * as the join path already does under 0243 and 0247.
+			 */
+			dev_info(wiphy_dev(mac->hw->wiphy),
+				 "one-shot passive WLAN bss notice: len=%zu seq=%u body=%02x%02x%02x%02x\n",
+				 bytes, packet[5], bytes > 8 ? packet[8] : 0,
+				 bytes > 9 ? packet[9] : 0, bytes > 10 ? packet[10] : 0,
+				 bytes > 11 ? packet[11] : 0);
+			return 0;
 		default:
 			dev_info(wiphy_dev(mac->hw->wiphy),
 				 "one-shot passive WLAN unknown event: len=%zu id=0x%02x seq=%u\n",
